WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.740
Shine a light into a little cell of
smoke and look through a microscope.

2
00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:09.010
The specks of smoke jitter
along jerky, random paths.

3
00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:13.540
Something invisible keeps knocking
them, first one way, then another.

4
00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:16.300
No single knock can be predicted.

5
00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:21.080
Yet a gas pushes on its container with
a steady pressure we can calculate.

6
00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:24.020
How can random hits add up to that?

7
00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:29.050
In this mission, you'll follow one molecule
bouncing back and forth inside a cube,

8
00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:30.840
and track its momentum.

9
00:00:30.890 --> 00:00:35.080
Then you'll use the kinetic theory
equation to find how fast the molecules in

10
00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:36.790
the air are moving.

11
00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:42.370
Your mission: explain how random molecular
hits add up to a pressure you can calculate.
